WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
An X-ray image is a shadow.

2
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.960
X-rays pass through the
body onto a detector.

3
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.070
Bone shows up white, with sharp edges.

4
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.510
Air in the lungs shows up dark.

5
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.810
But most soft organs, packed side by side,

6
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.490
barely show at all.

7
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.540
What makes bone stand out,
when soft organs do not?

8
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:25.790
In this mission, you'll meet four ways an
X-ray photon can be stopped or scattered,

9
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.250
and see how a beam fades, layer by layer.

10
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:34.380
Then you'll see how a CT scanner turns
readings from every angle into slices,

11
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.050
at roughly 500 times the
dose of a chest X-ray.

12
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: explain why bone casts a
sharp shadow while most soft organs barely

13
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.510
show.
